gal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{G}{G}","name":"Rumbling Baloth","oracle_id":"3191c6ca-4d25-4ba3-bfe1-4aeab1295573","oracle_text":"","power":"4","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-07-17","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Beast"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Harness by Force can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell or ability allows you to cast a strive spell without paying its mana cost, you must pay the additional costs for any targets beyond the first.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If all of the spell's targets are illegal when the spell tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. If one or more of its targets are legal when it tries to resolve, the spell will resolve and affect only those legal targets. It will have no effect on any illegal targets.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If such a spell is copied, and the effect that copies the spell allows a player to choose new targets for the copy, the number of targets can't be changed. The player may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, the player can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana cost and mana value of strive spells don't change no matter how many targets they have. Strive abilities affect only what you pay.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose how many targets each spell with a strive ability has and what those targets are as you cast it. It's legal to cast such a spell with no targets, although this is rarely a good idea. You can't choose the same target more than once for a single strive spell.","oracle_id":"8c7e2596-6c21-4ce0-95dc-5b4dccb4090a","published_at":"2014-04-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with Phyrexian mana symbols in its mana cost is each color that appears in that mana cost, regardless of how that cost may have been paid.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Aggression can target any creature an opponent controls, even one that's untapped.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As you cast a spell or activate an activated ability with one or more Phyrexian mana symbols in its cost, you choose how to pay for each Phyrexian mana symbol at the same time you would choose modes or choose a value for X.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you're at 1 life or less, you can't pay 2 life.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Phyrexian mana is not a new color. Players can't produce Phyrexian mana.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To calculate the mana value of a card with Phyrexian mana symbols in its cost, count each Phyrexian mana symbol as 1.","oracle_id":"9d7624ea-ffff-470b-928b-bbac66ddbd1c","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it. However, if you gain control of a creature enchanted by an Aura with umbra armor and that creature would be destroyed that turn, instead the Aura will be destroyed and the creature will survive.","oracle_id":"d96763a0-6a6e-4520-899a-468b4bb307c8","published_at":"2012-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Mass Mutiny can target untapped creatures.","oracle_id":"d96763a0-6a6e-4520-899a-468b4bb307c8","published_at":"2012-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The phrase \"up to one\" was inadvertently omitted from Mass Mutiny's rules text. The card has received errata to correct this.","oracle_id":"d96763a0-6a6e-4520-899a-468b4bb307c8","published_at":"2012-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can cast Mass Mutiny even if an opponent doesn't control any creatures. You simply won't choose a target for that opponent.","oracle_id":"d96763a0-6a6e-4520-899a-468b4bb307c8","published_at":"2012-06-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
